  "description": "Interactive 3D figure for force (বল) and its two kinds, স্পর্শ বল and অস্পর্শ বল, book page 67, topic 3.1.2. The page's five examples, one at a time, real size: a truck crane lifts a concrete block (ক্রেন দিয়ে ভারী জিনিস তোলা), a student pushes a trolley (ধাক্কা দেওয়া), friction stops a sliding crate (ঘর্ষণ), a football let go falls (মাধ্যাকর্ষণ বল) and a magnet brought by a hand pulls an iron nail (চুম্বকের আকর্ষণ). Press চালাও or touch the picture: the force acts, its orange arrow appears where it acts with its name, and where it meets the body is marked: a hollow blue ring round the place where something touches, a dashed violet bracket across the empty gap. The first time it stops at that moment and the student puts the example in the right box (স্পর্শ বল or অস্পর্শ বল); the book's definition of force lights the part that applies (a body at rest starts moving, or a moving body's velocity changes) and a readout shows the velocity (m/s and its direction). Slowed-down examples say so. Test tab: 5 questions with new cases in 3D (a rope pulling a cart, a parachute, a comb lifting paper: which kind and why), what a force is doing to a moving body, how the first law tells a force is acting, and which book example is the same kind. Phone-first, Bangla.",
